  "body": "## Result and exact scope\n\nPublish the complete five-segment counterexample and its full independent audit plus separate narrow analytic audit for problem 30001739. Disposition: **ACCEPTED_COMPLETE_COUNTEREXAMPLE** in the documented characteristic-zero p-adic smooth admissible complex scope. This is AI-assisted mathematical-audit acceptance, not conventional human peer review or journal acceptance.\n\nFor F=Q_3 and its unramified quadratic extension E, let pi be the Langlands quotient of the GL_15(E) standard module with ordered segments [4,6], [2,5], [3,3], [1,4], [0,2]. It is tau-invariant and noninduced (not itself an entire proper parabolic induction). For k=1, both Hermitian-form multiplicities vanish, so the target's total is **0 rather than 2**.\n\nThe proof uses complete 16-element Hom bases in three orders, holomorphic invertible transports for the two nested swaps, and necessary linked-pair coefficient constraints forming E-D-B-A-C-E. Noninducedness is certified by all **15** exact singleton Hall obstructions, with a ladder side in every partition. The highest-risk analytic steps passed the separate audit.\n\nFLO equation (4.5) is corrected to printed **p.225**; the rank-one kernel is explicitly the kernel of **unnormalized forward M**, equal to the image of **reverse normalized N**. General maximal-kernel generation is not used. The multiplicity conclusion depends on the cited published FLO, JPSS and LM theorems. The finite scripts do not compute Hom spaces.\n\n## Literature and attribution\n\nThe same accepted vanishing also contradicts FLO Conjecture 6.12 (p.246), since the individually tau-invariant Langlands data have tau-Witt index zero by FLO pp.214\u2013215. This is a same-scope consequence, not a separate independent-discovery claim. [FLO published record](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10240-012-0040-z).\n\nA bounded 50-query literature comparison verified no exact or translated/twisted-equivalent predecessor and no contrary established theorem. **Priority remains unestablished.** Luo\u2013Zha's related kernel-generation counterexample was announced in the [May 13, 2025 workshop program](https://hkumath.hku.hk/MathWWW/event/2025/Workshop_Program.pdf) and [published online July 5, 2026](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11464-025-0256-0). Their full paper remains uninspected: neither exact duplication nor unrelatedness is asserted. No all-local-fields or novelty claim is made.\n\n## Contents and limits\n\nThis is an additive, target-only 44-file source-free delivery under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30001739/`:\n\n- Current complete proof, contextual corrections, both full mathematical audit reports, diagnostic-validation narrative, exact target model, and all 15 Hall certificates.\n- Four complete finite checkers: authored set-based Hall and scalar/parity checks, full independent audit checks, and separate exact-rational scalar checks of all 10 pairs at q=3,9 and both signs (40 rows; 30 order conditions).\n- Public-only citation/PDF-hash/inspection metadata and the bounded priority report, public search history and match results.\n- Isolated replay adapter, full raw mode-specific reference outputs, strict manifest/verifier, actual finite mutants and separately categorized publication controls.\n\nNo source PDFs or source text, dataset contents, private sources, private coordination, identifying metadata for excluded private files, wholesale source archives, or full superseded provisional proof are included. All 173 original files remain unchanged. The author is frozen at 2/5 proof approaches; no new proof approach is introduced by publication. `QUEUE.md` and all unrelated repository content are unchanged.\n\n## Fresh verification\n\nNormal Python, -O and -OO each passed as actual UID/EUID1000 with files 0444 and packet directories 0555:\n\n- 4 positive full-output finite checker runs and 6 actual mathematical algorithm/hypothesis source mutants, all rejected for their intended exact reasons.\n- Separately: 61 integrity mutations, 77 strict-schema/scope controls and 34 direct output-comparator controls.\n- 48 actual denied-write probes per mode, requiring PermissionError/errno13.\n- Complete stdout/stderr byte equality and recursively exact JSON identities, counts, types and reasons; no normalization or PASS-only acceptance. Exact captured inner checker streams are retained verbatim with byte counts/hashes and compared against fixed references, alongside the entire raw adapter output. Strict inner parsing rejects duplicate keys, nonfinite/overflow values, malformed JSON and trailing content.\n- Targeted outer and direct-inner controls reject whitespace-only changes and duplicate-key JSON yielding the same ordinarily decoded object; these are publication-validation controls, separate from mathematical mutations.\n- Hostile-import complete-baseline output equality, with no hostile sentinel and unchanged whole-delivery before/after hashes.\n- A held-out fresh `git apply` of the exact additive diff reproduced every delivered byte and the **entire raw control-harness output** in all three modes.\n\nActual mathematical mutation coverage is distinct from integrity/schema coverage. Repeated integrity/hostile replays do not add mathematical coverage. The four adapted checkers preserve all mathematical operations and remove writes; the installed-dependency adapter verifies SymPy 1.14.0 and mpmath 1.3.0 from the trusted interpreter-prefix site-packages location while requiring -I -S -B. No site hooks or environment/current-directory imports are allowed. Installed dependency code is part of the trusted runtime, not bundled or independently certified here.\n\n## External trust anchor\n\nAuthenticate the bootstrap from this externally reviewed body before running it. The bootstrap pins the entire manifest, verifier and control harness; the manifest pins every other delivered file. The manifest excludes itself and the bootstrap, avoiding self-hash circularity. Final external and held-out replay receipts remain outside the public delivery.\n\n- `BOOTSTRAP.py`: SHA-256 `6a55d39218fc77266c46aafef424127933afe54d493593c4745bc53e97cafcd4`, 2356 bytes\n- `PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.json`: SHA-256 `a51fbcd5c73671f0bd0a5d35ff58fe83abc71a2cdef279d31bc04062e79f904d`, 6970 bytes\n- `verify_publication.py`: SHA-256 `ba39260ecd9c6fd126676e377dcb95e64635d22204abd3562376432fdef3b787`, 404501 bytes\n- `MUTATION_TESTS.py`: SHA-256 `293dd972029b93a833915d030a85ccd003527f55ad0dd3a6ad6dbaad31471169`, 20437 bytes\n\nCopy that authenticated bootstrap outside the packet, then run `python -I -S -B EXTERNAL_BOOTSTRAP.py --controls PACKET`, also with -O and -OO, as UID/EUID1000 against read-only files/directories. Every verifier failure is a failure, not an optional skip.\n\nBase commit: `6ca1e663ab556636a3c2a9b67a96274ef95e8bab`; base tree: `a675bbb4eb340ad8a83943d490404c5f9585c0e1`. Fresh main, immutable commit/tree and exact-ref target absence were checked. Draft only; no merge or deployment requested.\n",
